   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *          functionalities of the Serial peripheral interface (SPI):
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           + Data transfers functions
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           + Hardware CRC Calculation
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           + DMA transfers management
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management 
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *           
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** @verbatim
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ===================================================================
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****                   ##### How to use this driver #####
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ===================================================================
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..]
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable peripheral clock using the following functions 
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB2Periph_SPI1, ENABLE) for SPI1
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI2, ENABLE) for SPI2
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI3, ENABLE) for SPI3
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI3, ENABLE) for SPI4
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI3, ENABLE) for SPI5
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI3, ENABLE) for SPI6.
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable SCK, MOSI, MISO and NSS GPIO clocks using RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd()
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc1nuMuI.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        function. In I2S mode, if an external clock source is used then the I2S 
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        CKIN pin GPIO clock should also be enabled.
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Peripherals alternate function: 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Connect the pin to the desired peripherals' Alternate Function (AF) 
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             using GPIO_PinAFConfig() function
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Configure the desired pin in alternate function by: 
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AF
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Select the type, pull-up/pull-down and output speed via GPIO_PuPd, 
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             GPIO_OType and GPIO_Speed members
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Call GPIO_Init() function In I2S mode, if an external clock source is 
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             used then the I2S CKIN pin should be also configured in Alternate 
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             function Push-pull pull-up mode. 
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****           
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Program the Polarity, Phase, First Data, Baud Rate Prescaler, Slave 
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        Management, Peripheral Mode and CRC Polynomial values using the SPI_Init()
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        function.
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        In I2S mode, program the Mode, Standard, Data Format, MCLK Output, Audio 
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        frequency and Polarity using I2S_Init() function. For I2S mode, make sure 
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        that either:
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) I2S PLL is configured using the functions 
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             RCC_I2SCLKConfig(RCC_I2S2CLKSource_PLLI2S), RCC_PLLI2SCmd(ENABLE) and 
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             RCC_GetFlagStatus(RCC_FLAG_PLLI2SRDY); or 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) External clock source is configured using the function 
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             RCC_I2SCLKConfig(RCC_I2S2CLKSource_Ext) and after setting correctly 
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             the define constant I2S_EXTERNAL_CLOCK_VAL in the stm32f4xx_conf.h file. 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable the NVIC and the corresponding interrupt using the function 
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        SPI_ITConfig() if you need to use interrupt mode. 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) When using the DMA mode 
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Configure the DMA using DMA_Init() function
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Active the needed channel Request using SPI_I2S_DMACmd() function
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable the SPI using the SPI_Cmd() function or enable the I2S using
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        I2S_Cmd().
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable the DMA using the DMA_Cmd() function when using DMA mode. 
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Optionally, you can enable/configure the following parameters without
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        re-initialization (i.e there is no need to call again SPI_Init() function):
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) When bidirectional mode (SPI_Direction_1Line_Rx or SPI_Direction_1Line_Tx)
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             is programmed as Data direction parameter using the SPI_Init() function
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             it can be possible to switch between SPI_Direction_Tx or SPI_Direction_Rx
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             using the SPI_BiDirectionalLineConfig() function.
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) When SPI_NSS_Soft is selected as Slave Select Management parameter 
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             using the SPI_Init() function it can be possible to manage the 
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             NSS internal signal using the SPI_NSSInternalSoftwareConfig() function.
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Reconfigure the data size using the SPI_DataSizeConfig() function  
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (++) Enable or disable the SS output using the SPI_SSOutputCmd() function  
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****     (#) To use the CRC Hardware calculation feature refer to the Peripheral 
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****         CRC hardware Calculation subsection.
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****      
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] It is possible to use SPI in I2S full duplex mode, in this case, each SPI 
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       peripheral is able to manage sending and receiving data simultaneously
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc1nuMuI.s 			page 3


  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       using two data lines. Each SPI peripheral has an extended block called I2Sxext
  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       (ie. I2S2ext for SPI2 and I2S3ext for SPI3).
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       The extension block is not a full SPI IP, it is used only as I2S slave to
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       implement full duplex mode. The extension block uses the same clock sources
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       as its master.          
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       To configure I2S full duplex you have to:
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****               
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       (#) Configure SPIx in I2S mode (I2S_Init() function) as described above. 
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****              
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       (#) Call the I2S_FullDuplexConfig() function using the same structure passed to  
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****           I2S_Init() function.
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****               
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       (#) Call I2S_Cmd() for SPIx then for its extended block.
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       (#) To configure interrupts or DMA requests and to get/clear flag status, 
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****           use I2Sxext instance for the extension block.
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****                
 104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] Functions that can be called with I2Sxext instances are: I2S_Cmd(), 
 105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_FullDuplexConfig(), SPI_I2S_ReceiveData(), SPI_I2S_SendData(), 
 106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       SPI_I2S_DMACmd(), SPI_I2S_ITConfig(), SPI_I2S_GetFlagStatus(), 
 107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       SPI_I2S_ClearFlag(), SPI_I2S_GetITStatus() and SPI_I2S_ClearITPendingBit().
 108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****                    
 109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       Example: To use SPI3 in Full duplex mode (SPI3 is Master Tx, I2S3ext is Slave Rx):
 110:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****               
 111:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_SPI3, ENABLE);   
 112:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_StructInit(&I2SInitStruct);
 113:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2SInitStruct.Mode = I2S_Mode_MasterTx;     
 114:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_Init(SPI3, &I2SInitStruct);
 115:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_FullDuplexConfig(SPI3ext, &I2SInitStruct)
 116:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_Cmd(SPI3, ENABLE);
 117:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       I2S_Cmd(SPI3ext, ENABLE);
 118:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       ...
 119:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       while (SPI_I2S_GetFlagStatus(SPI2, SPI_FLAG_TXE) == RESET)
 120:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       {}
 121:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       SPI_I2S_SendData(SPI3, txdata[i]);
 122:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       ...  
 123:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       while (SPI_I2S_GetFlagStatus(I2S3ext, SPI_FLAG_RXNE) == RESET)
 124:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       {}
 125:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       rxdata[i] = SPI_I2S_ReceiveData(I2S3ext);
 126:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       ...          
 127:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****                 
 128:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..]       
 129:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) In I2S mode: if an external clock is used as source clock for the I2S,  
 130:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        then the define I2S_EXTERNAL_CLOCK_VAL in file stm32f4xx_conf.h should 
 131:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        be enabled and set to the value of the source clock frequency (in Hz).
 132:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    
 133:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) In SPI mode: To use the SPI TI mode, call the function SPI_TIModeCmd() 
 134:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        just after calling the function SPI_Init().
 135:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   
 136:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** @endverbatim  
 137:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *                                  
