 853:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] This section provides a set of functions allowing to manage the SPI CRC hardware 
 854:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       calculation
 855:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 856:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] SPI communication using CRC is possible through the following procedure:
 857:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Program the Data direction, Polarity, Phase, First Data, Baud Rate Prescaler, 
 858:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        Slave Management, Peripheral Mode and CRC Polynomial values using the SPI_Init()
 859:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        function.
 860:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable the CRC calculation using the SPI_CalculateCRC() function.
 861:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Enable the SPI using the SPI_Cmd() function
 862:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) Before writing the last data to the TX buffer, set the CRCNext bit using the 
 863:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        SPI_TransmitCRC() function to indicate that after transmission of the last 
 864:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        data, the CRC should be transmitted.
 865:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) After transmitting the last data, the SPI transmits the CRC. The SPI_CR1_CRCNEXT
 866:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****         bit is reset. The CRC is also received and compared against the SPI_RXCRCR 
 867:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****         value. 
 868:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****         If the value does not match, the SPI_FLAG_CRCERR flag is set and an interrupt
 869:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****         can be generated when the SPI_I2S_IT_ERR interrupt is enabled.
 870:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 871:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..]
 872:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) It is advised not to read the calculated CRC values during the communication.
 873:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 874:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) When the SPI is in slave mode, be careful to enable CRC calculation only 
 875:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        when the clock is stable, that is, when the clock is in the steady state. 
 876:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        If not, a wrong CRC calculation may be done. In fact, the CRC is sensitive 
 877:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        to the SCK slave input clock as soon as CRCEN is set, and this, whatever 
 878:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        the value of the SPE bit.
 879:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 880:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) With high bitrate frequencies, be careful when transmitting the CRC.
 881:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        As the number of used CPU cycles has to be as low as possible in the CRC 
 882:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        transfer phase, it is forbidden to call software functions in the CRC 
 883:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        transmission sequence to avoid errors in the last data and CRC reception. 
 884:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        In fact, CRCNEXT bit has to be written before the end of the transmission/reception 
 885:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        of the last data.
 886:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 887:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) For high bit rate frequencies, it is advised to use the DMA mode to avoid the
 888:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        degradation of the SPI speed performance due to CPU accesses impacting the 
 889:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        SPI bandwidth.
 890:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 891:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) When the STM32F4xx is configured as slave and the NSS hardware mode is 
 892:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        used, the NSS pin needs to be kept low between the data phase and the CRC 
 893:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        phase.
 894:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 895:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) When the SPI is configured in slave mode with the CRC feature enabled, CRC
 896:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        calculation takes place even if a high level is applied on the NSS pin. 
 897:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        This may happen for example in case of a multi-slave environment where the 
 898:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        communication master addresses slaves alternately.
 899:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 900:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) Between a slave de-selection (high level on NSS) and a new slave selection 
 901:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (low level on NSS), the CRC value should be cleared on both master and slave
 902:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        sides in order to resynchronize the master and slave for their respective 
 903:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        CRC calculation.
 904:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 905:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (@) To clear the CRC, follow the procedure below:
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc1nuMuI.s 			page 36


 906:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (#@) Disable SPI using the SPI_Cmd() function
 907:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (#@) Disable the CRC calculation using the SPI_CalculateCRC() function.
 908:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (#@) Enable the CRC calculation using the SPI_CalculateCRC() function.
 909:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (#@) Enable SPI using the SPI_Cmd() function.
 910:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
 911:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** @endverbatim
 912:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   * @{
 913:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   */
