1047:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** /** @defgroup SPI_Group5 Interrupts and flags management functions
1048:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  *  @brief   Interrupts and flags management functions
1049:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   *
1050:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** @verbatim   
1051:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ===============================================================================
1052:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             ##### Interrupts and flags management functions #####
1053:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ===============================================================================  
1054:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  
1055:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] This section provides a set of functions allowing to configure the SPI Interrupts 
1056:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       sources and check or clear the flags or pending bits status.
1057:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       The user should identify which mode will be used in his application to manage 
1058:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       the communication: Polling mode, Interrupt mode or DMA mode. 
1059:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****     
1060:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  *** Polling Mode ***
1061:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ====================
1062:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** [..] In Polling Mode, the SPI/I2S communication can be managed by 9 flags:
1063:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_I2S_FLAG_TXE : to indicate the status of the transmit buffer register
1064:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_I2S_FLAG_RXNE : to indicate the status of the receive buffer register
1065:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_I2S_FLAG_BSY : to indicate the state of the communication layer of the SPI.
1066:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_FLAG_CRCERR : to indicate if a CRC Calculation error occur              
1067:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_FLAG_MODF : to indicate if a Mode Fault error occur
1068:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) SPI_I2S_FLAG_OVR : to indicate if an Overrun error occur
1069:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) I2S_FLAG_TIFRFE: to indicate a Frame Format error occurs.
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc1nuMuI.s 			page 42


1070:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) I2S_FLAG_UDR: to indicate an Underrun error occurs.
1071:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (#) I2S_FLAG_CHSIDE: to indicate Channel Side.
1072:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1073:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   (@) Do not use the BSY flag to handle each data transmission or reception. It is
1074:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       better to use the TXE and RXNE flags instead.
1075:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1076:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] In this Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
1077:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) FlagStatus SPI_I2S_GetFlagStatus(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint16_t SPI_I2S_FLAG);
1078:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) void SPI_I2S_ClearFlag(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint16_t SPI_I2S_FLAG);
1079:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1080:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  *** Interrupt Mode ***
1081:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ======================
1082:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] In Interrupt Mode, the SPI communication can be managed by 3 interrupt sources
1083:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****       and 7 pending bits: 
1084:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) Pending Bits:
1085:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_TXE : to indicate the status of the transmit buffer register
1086:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_RXNE : to indicate the status of the receive buffer register
1087:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_IT_CRCERR : to indicate if a CRC Calculation error occur (available in SPI mode onl
1088:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_IT_MODF : to indicate if a Mode Fault error occur (available in SPI mode only)
1089:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_OVR : to indicate if an Overrun error occur
1090:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) I2S_IT_UDR : to indicate an Underrun Error occurs (available in I2S mode only).
1091:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) I2S_FLAG_TIFRFE : to indicate a Frame Format error occurs (available in TI mode only).
1092:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1093:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) Interrupt Source:
1094:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_TXE: specifies the interrupt source for the Tx buffer empty 
1095:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             interrupt.  
1096:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_RXNE : specifies the interrupt source for the Rx buffer not 
1097:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****             empty interrupt.
1098:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        (##) SPI_I2S_IT_ERR : specifies the interrupt source for the errors interrupt.
1099:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] In this Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
1101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) void SPI_I2S_ITConfig(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint8_t SPI_I2S_IT, FunctionalState NewState);
1102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) ITStatus SPI_I2S_GetITStatus(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint8_t SPI_I2S_IT);
1103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) void SPI_I2S_ClearITPendingBit(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint8_t SPI_I2S_IT);
1104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  *** DMA Mode ***
1106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  ================
1107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] In DMA Mode, the SPI communication can be managed by 2 DMA Channel requests:
1108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) SPI_I2S_DMAReq_Tx: specifies the Tx buffer DMA transfer request
1109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (#) SPI_I2S_DMAReq_Rx: specifies the Rx buffer DMA transfer request
1110:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1111:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****  [..] In this Mode it is advised to use the following function:
1112:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****    (+) void SPI_I2S_DMACmd(SPI_TypeDef* SPIx, uint16_t SPI_I2S_DMAReq, FunctionalState 
1113:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****        NewState);
1114:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
1115:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** @endverbatim
1116:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   * @{
1117:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c ****   */
1118:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_spi.c **** 
